  "final_message": "Waiting for the test execution to complete.The test execution is in progress. I will inspect the results shortly.\nWaiting for the test execution to complete.\nThe tests are currently executing. I am waiting for the test run to finish.\nThe command is running in the background. I am waiting for its completion.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/GEMINI.md).\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly\n\n- **ARCH-4 Compliance**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is consumed by external services in other repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). ARCH-4 mandates:\n  > *`OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.*\n- **Breaking External Consumers**: Removing `channel` directly is a breaking schema change that breaks deployed consumers expecting `channel` on schema version 3.\n- **Model Coupling**: Removing `channel` from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model would prevent [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) from providing the field when generating events for downstream services.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\nTo retire `channel` in compliance with architecture governance:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n2. Coordinate deprecation with the `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` teams to ensure downstream consumers stop reading it.\n3. Introduce a new schema version (v4) once consumer deprecation periods conclude.\n",
